UID:74b876a7ef2e144f@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260922T051006Z
SEQUENCE:2026092205
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 6:00 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 5:45 PM.\nOn stage: 7:00 PM–7:45 PM.\nACT I 
 Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — pr
 oduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time danc
 ers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Tim
 e.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiv
 ing and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are cal
 led unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedul
 e\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mast
 er: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N
 7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Commandants ***\nSol
 diers: Commandant — Costume (you provide): Black Seamless Tights\, Bla
 ck Camisole Leotard\; Shoes: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Men's Light St
 age Makeup Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: Male: Hair out of the eyes Female:
  High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): White Gloves\; Prop (BA
  provides): White gun\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Powder
  matching skintone\n• Light brown eye shadow applied to the crease wit
 h an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara. 
 No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dan
 cer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Red or Dark Red 
 lipstick\nMen's Stage Makeup:\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner - apply fro
 m corner to corner\n• Brown or tan under cheek bone to create shadow a
 nd accentuate the jaw line\n• Brown eye liner around lips and nude/fle
 sh colored lipstick\n• *Men will not look like they are wearing makeup
 . It will help the face be seen from the stage.\nDancers of Color may we
 ar flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelin
 es:\n• Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damag
 e to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event 
 of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\
 n• Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes
  by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the floor while in
  costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any co
 stume or accessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while in costume and s
 hall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during 
 its removal\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while 
 in costume\n• Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n• 
 Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the ex
 ception of water\n• Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressin
 g rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used to secure he
 ad pieces and wigs following their use\n• Return all headpieces to the
 ir assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Ar
 kansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored 
 drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
